    <name>
      <text>Determining the exact value of an angle</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>
Determine the exact value of  \(\sin({@angle@}^\circ)\).
</p>

<p>Give your answer in simplest exact form.</p>

<p>
[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]
</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>

<p><strong>Step 1: Identify the reference angle.</strong></p>

<p>The angle is negative, so it represents a clockwise rotation. We can find a positive coterminal angle by adding \(360^\circ\):</p>

<p>
\({@angle@}+360^\circ = {@angle+360@}^\circ.\)
</p>

<p>The corresponding reference angle is \(60^\circ\), \(45^\circ\), or \(30^\circ\), depending on the given angle.</p>

<p><strong>Step 2: Determine the sign of sine.</strong></p>

<p>The terminal arm lies in a quadrant where sine is negative. Therefore, the value of \(\sin({@angle@}^\circ)\) must be negative.</p>

<p><strong>Step 3: Use the special-angle value.</strong></p>

<p>Using the reference angle and the exact values of the trigonometric ratios, we obtain:</p>

<p>
\(\sin({@angle@}^\circ)={@ta@}.\)
</p>

<p><strong>Therefore, the exact value is:</strong></p>

<p>
\(\boxed{{@ta@}}\)
</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
