        <truefeedback format="html">
          <text><![CDATA[<p>Your answer suggests that you may have treated the negative angle as a positive angle.</p>

<p>Remember that a negative angle represents a clockwise rotation. We can find a positive coterminal angle by adding \(360^\circ\):</p>

<p style="text-align: center;">
\(
{@angle@}^\circ+360^\circ={@coterminal@}^\circ.
\)
</p>

<p>The terminal arm therefore lies in Quadrant {@quadrant@}. Since sine is negative in Quadrants III and IV, the value of sine must be negative.</p>

<p>The reference angle is {@reference@}^\circ, so</p>

<p style="text-align: center;">
\(
\sin({@angle@}^\circ)=-\sin({@reference@}^\circ)
={@ta@}.
\)
</p>]]></text>
